 suicide ended up  committing self-harm because they  weren't getting the basic support that  they required we also heard from people  who  couldn't afford the basics in life who  had lost their loved one who bought in  um who was the main breadwinner and  simply couldn't afford to stay in their  house they or others who couldn't afford  to adapt their houses to take a  wheelchair that they were then in so  those basic things those basic  uh that basic level of support we found  was lacking so what we're calling for  today is for the government to implement  its promise  to consult on a survivor's chart and  that's a fancy  way of saying a set of guarantees legal  guarantees on things like compensation  on things like  access to mental health support so that  when this awful thing happens when this  attack on our state  takes place that those people are  properly looked after and supported  are there any other countries to which  we can look to for for inspiration and  all of this we've had our fair share of  terror attacks in this country so too  have others however yeah so what we did  in order to inform this this charter  back back in 2019  uh the government boris johnson  committed to consult on a survivors  charter and so what we've done over the  last couple of years is to work on an  analysis looking at france looking at  belgium looking at australia new zealand  israel us canada and looking to try to  understand what are they getting right  that we're getting wrong what are we  getting right that they're getting wrong  and what we found out from that was that  there are some countries places like  france places like belgium where they  just have a completely different and  higher level of support and that's  partly because of the individual areas  of support that they offer but it's also  that they have a different attitude they  see terror attacks  not as an unfortunate accident that  happens to an individual like a car  accident which is the way that we tend  to see it in the uk  um but as an attack on the state that  requires a response from the state so in  france for example um the survivors are  often treated as if they are our  veterans people who are unwilling  veterans of a  of a war and that the state has a  particular responsibility so we think  there are real things that we can learn  and that will both have an impact on the  survivors themselves but we'll also send  out a incredibly strong message that in  the face of terrorism we will look after  each other  brendan cox we have to leave it there as  we are just about out of time but really  appreciate it we'll keep your fingers  fingers crossed that the government  listens  stay we are we will have much more from  in and around ukraine coming next  [Music]
 

